LONGEST VALID PARENTHESES (Stack + DP ⭐)

This problem is different from “Minimum Remove Parentheses”.
Here we do NOT remove, we find the longest valid substring.

📌 Problem Statement

Given a string s containing only '(' and ')', find the length of the longest valid (well-formed) parentheses substring.

🔹 Example 1
Input:  "(()"
Output: 2
Explanation: "()"

🔹 Example 2
Input:  ")()())"
Output: 4
Explanation: "()()"

🔹 Example 3
Input:  ""
Output: 0

🧠 Key Insight (Interview Favorite Question ❗)

A valid parentheses substring must:

Start after an invalid )

Have balanced opening & closing brackets

We use a stack of indices, not characters.

🛠️ Algorithm (Stack-Based – Most Common)
Step 1: Initialize stack

Push -1 initially
👉 This acts as a base index

Step 2: Traverse string

For each character at index i:

If '(' → push index

If ')':

pop stack

If stack becomes empty → push current index

Else → calculate length = i - stack.peek()

Step 3: Track maximum length
⏱ Complexity

Time: O(n)

Space: O(n)

☕ Java Code (Interview-Ready)
class Solution {
    public int longestValidParentheses(String s) {
        Stack<Integer> stack = new Stack<>();
        stack.push(-1); // base for valid substring
        int maxLen = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            char c = s.charAt(i);

            if (c == '(') {
                stack.push(i);
            } else {
                stack.pop();

                if (stack.isEmpty()) {
                    stack.push(i);
                } else {
                    maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, i - stack.peek());
                }
            }
        }

        return maxLen;
    }
}

